# ── Supabase-backed static build (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify) ─────────────────
# Set both and the app becomes a serverless openGym: email/password auth via
# Supabase Auth and the whole per-user state blob synced through the `state`
# table (schema in supabase/migrations/0001_state.sql). Without these vars the
# build is the normal self-hosted client.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste the "anon" / publishable key from Dashboard → Settings → API
#
# Exercise media for a static deploy (no media container): point at the upstream
# dataset on a CDN, like the demo workflow does.
# VITE_IMG_BASE=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/hasaneyldrm/exercises-dataset@7455efae41b330c265e7cd4b78dfa848e7ce5ebd/images/
# VITE_GIF_BASE=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/hasaneyldrm/exercises-dataset@7455efae41b330c265e7cd4b78dfa848e7ce5ebd/videos/

# The rest of this file documents the self-hosted (Docker) instance.
# ── Local testing (default) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Works out of the box on the machine running Docker. Open http://localhost:8080
RP_ID=localhost
ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080
WEB_PORT=8080
RP_NAME=openGym